---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { brand, legal } from '@data/site';
import { withBase } from '@utils/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description={`The terms that apply when you create an account or use ${brand.appName}.`}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <header class="legal-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1 class="h2">Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="faint">Effective {legal.effectiveDate}</p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Agreement</h2>
        <p>
          {brand.appName} is a workout tracking app for iPhone and Apple Watch. By creating an
          account or using {brand.appName} (the &ldquo;Service&rdquo;), you agree to these terms. If
          you don't agree, please don't use the Service.
        </p>

        <h2>Licence</h2>
        <p>
          You are granted a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to use {
            brand.appName
          }. You may not copy, decompile, reverse-engineer or redistribute the app.
        </p>

        <h2>Your account</h2>
        <p>
          {brand.appName} requires an account — email and password, or Sign in with Apple — so your
          training history can sync between your iPhone and Apple Watch.
        </p>
        <p>
          Keep your credentials to yourself. You are responsible for everything logged under your
          account. If you think someone else got in, email{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${brand.email}`}>{brand.email}</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can delete your account, and the data attached to it, from Settings → Account → Delete
          Account. It is permanent.
        </p>

        <h2>Your content</h2>
        <p>
          Your workouts, routines, custom exercises and notes are <strong>yours</strong>. We claim no
          ownership over anything you enter into the app.
        </p>
        <p>
          You give us permission to store and sync your content only so the app can work — so it
          reaches your other device and comes back to you. That permission ends when you delete the
          content or your account.
        </p>
        <p>
          {brand.appName} syncs through your account to our servers.
          <strong>It is not a backup service.</strong> Keep your own copy of anything that matters: Settings
          → Export Data gives you a CSV of your workout history.
        </p>
        <p>{brand.appName} has no social features. Nothing you log is visible to other users.</p>

        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>Please don't:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Use the Service for anything unlawful</li>
          <li>Try to reach anyone else's account or data</li>
          <li>Reverse-engineer or decompile the app</li>
          <li>Get around subscription limits or tamper with purchases</li>
          <li>Probe, scrape, overload or disrupt the Service or its infrastructure</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Health and safety</h2>

        <div class="callout">
          <strong>
            {brand.appName} is a training log. It is not a medical device and gives no medical, nutritional
            or coaching advice.
          </strong>
          You train at your own risk.
        </div>

        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Talk to a doctor before starting or changing a training programme</strong> —
            especially if you have a medical condition or injury, are pregnant, or take medication.
          </li>
          <li>
            Exercise can cause injury. How you train, how much you lift, and your own form and
            safety are your responsibility. Stop and get medical help if you feel unwell or
            experience pain.
          </li>
          <li>
            Everything the app shows you — analytics, records, streaks, estimates — is derived from
            what you entered. Don't make medical decisions from it.
          </li>
          <li>
            Voice logging can mishear you, especially in a loud gym. <strong>Check what got logged.</strong>
            You can undo a dictated set right away or edit it later.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Subscriptions and payment</h2>
        <p>
          {brand.appName} is free to use, with a limit of <strong>5 routines</strong> and{' '}
          <strong>25 custom exercises</strong>. Detailed analytics, the personal-record showcase, and
          data export are locked on the free plan.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>{brand.appName} Pro</strong> removes those limits and unlocks those features. It comes
          as a monthly or annual plan, and prices are shown in the app before you buy.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Apple handles the payment</strong>, not us. We never see your card details.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Your subscription renews automatically</strong> unless you cancel at least 24 hours
            before the period ends. Apple charges you within 24 hours of renewal.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>To cancel</strong>, go to iOS Settings → your name → Subscriptions. Cancelling stops
            future charges but doesn't refund the period you're in.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Refunds come from Apple</strong>, under Apple's policies — we usually can't issue
            them. Ask at{' '}
            <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              reportaproblem.apple.com
            </a>.
          </li>
          <li>You can restore a past purchase from Settings → Restore Purchases at any time.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If your subscription ends, <strong>your data stays put.</strong> Pro features lock, and anything
          over the free limits stays in your account — you just can't add more until you're under the
          limit or subscribe again.
        </p>

        <h2>Warranty and liability</h2>
        <p>
          The Service is provided <strong>&ldquo;as is&rdquo;</strong>, without warranties of any
          kind, express or implied. We don't promise it will always work, always sync, or never lose
          data. <strong>Export your data if it matters to you.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, {brand.appName} and its suppliers are not liable for
          lost data, lost profits, or any indirect, incidental or consequential damages arising from
          your use of {brand.appName}.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some places don't allow these limits, so parts of this may not apply to you. Nothing here
          limits liability that can't legally be limited.
        </p>

        <h2>Ending things</h2>
        <p>You can stop using {brand.appName} and delete your account at any time.</p>
        <p>
          We may suspend or close your account if you seriously break these terms or if we're
          legally required to. If we shut the Service down entirely, we'll give you at least 30 days
          to export your data.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms. Material changes will be reflected in the effective date above,
          and we'll tell you in the app or by email first. Continued use of the Service after a
          change means you accept the updated terms.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${brand.email}`}>{brand.email}</a>. See also
          our <a href={withBase('/privacy')}>Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-head {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-l);
  }

  .legal-head > * + * {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .callout {
    padding: var(--space-s) var(--space-m);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--brand);
    border-radius: var(--radius-m);
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .callout strong {
    display: block;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 0.4em;
  }
</style>
